            </div>
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Answers…</th><th>One-line takeaway</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><a href="#s3-1"><strong>3.1</strong> Overview</a></td><td>What are the two halves?</td><td>Control plane decides; worker nodes run. You manage both.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#s3-2"><strong>3.2</strong> Control plane</a></td><td>What's the "brain"?</td><td>apiserver (door) · etcd (state) · scheduler (placement) · controllers (reconcile).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#s3-3"><strong>3.3</strong> Worker nodes</a></td><td>What's the "muscle"?</td><td>kubelet (agent) · kube-proxy (service routing) · runtime (runs containers).</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><a href="#s3-4"><strong>3.4</strong> Pod is born</a></td><td>How does a pod actually start?</td><td>kubectl → apiserver → etcd → controllers → scheduler → kubelet → Running.</td></tr>
