        <article class="chapter" id="appendix-g">
        <h2 class="chapter-title">📅 Appendix G · 10-Week CKA Learning Path</h2>
        <div class="chapter-meta">
            <span class="badge badge-appendix">APPENDIX</span>
            <span class="badge badge-reference">📋 REFERENCE</span>
        </div>
        <p class="chapter-lead">Week-by-week study roadmap from complete beginner to CKA-certified administrator. Designed for 8–12 hours of study per week alongside a full-time job.</p>

        <!-- Roadmap Visual -->
        <div class="diagram-container">
            <h4>10-Week CKA Learning Roadmap</h4>
            <div class="diagram-box">
                <pre>
  WEEK   PHASE            DIFFICULTY    FOCUS AREA
  ─────  ───────────────  ──────────    ─────────────────────────────────
   1     🟢 Foundation    ★☆☆☆☆        Docker basics, K8s concepts, setup
   2     🟢 Foundation    ★★☆☆☆        kubectl mastery, pods, namespaces

   3     🟡 Intermediate  ★★☆☆☆        Deployments, ReplicaSets, Services
   4     🟡 Intermediate  ★★★☆☆        ConfigMaps, Secrets, Volumes, PV/PVC
   5     🟡 Intermediate  ★★★☆☆        Scheduling: taints, affinity, DaemonSets
   6     🟡 Intermediate  ★★★☆☆        Networking: Services, Ingress, DNS, NetworkPolicy

   7     🟠 Advanced      ★★★★☆        RBAC, Security Contexts, ServiceAccounts
   8     🟠 Advanced      ★★★★☆        Cluster admin: kubeadm, upgrades, etcd backup

   9     🔴 Expert        ★★★★★        Troubleshooting deep-dive (30% of exam!)

  10     🎯 EXAM READY    ★★★★★        Mock exams, killer.sh, review weak areas

                    ──────── TAKE THE CKA EXAM ────────
                    66% to pass │ 1 free retake included
</pre>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Week 1 -->
        <div class="info-box note" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(34,197,94,0.08), rgba(16,185,129,0.08)); border-left: 4px solid #22c55e; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <h4>🟢 Week 1 — Foundation: Containers &amp; Kubernetes Concepts</h4>
            <div class="comparison-table" style="margin-top: 0.8rem;">
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th style="width:15%;">Day</th><th style="width:35%;">Topic</th><th style="width:15%;">Chapters</th><th>Hands-On</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>Day 1–2</td><td>Docker fundamentals: images, containers, Dockerfiles</td><td>Ch 1</td><td>Build easypj Docker image</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Day 3–4</td><td>Kubernetes architecture: control plane, worker nodes, etcd</td><td>Ch 2–3</td><td>Install minikube or kind</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Day 5–6</td><td>kubectl basics: get, describe, create, delete, apply</td><td>Ch 4</td><td>Deploy first pod, explore cluster</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Day 7</td><td><strong>Review + Lab:</strong> Deploy a multi-container pod</td><td>Ch 1–4</td><td>Killercoda beginner scenarios</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #86efac;"><strong>Goal:</strong> Comfortable running kubectl commands, understand pods, can explain K8s architecture on a whiteboard.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Week 2 -->
        <div class="info-box note" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(34,197,94,0.08), rgba(16,185,129,0.08)); border-left: 4px solid #22c55e; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
            <h4>🟢 Week 2 — Foundation: kubectl Mastery &amp; Core Objects</h4>
            <div class="comparison-table" style="margin-top: 0.8rem;">
                <table>
